From: nabu port
Subject: [PATCH 0013] nabu: processors are booted at registration (XNU 12377)

The full macOS 27.3 kernelcache under QEMU (series 0001-0012) stopped in
NabuCPU::startAll with "NABU CPU: processor_start cpu=0 failed: 5":
processor_start() is now processor_start_from_kext(), a no-op returning
KERN_FAILURE. Calling processor_boot() instead then panicked "processor 0
already booted": without USE_APPLEARMSMP, ml_processor_register() boots the
processor itself (osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c). startAll now only waits
for each CPU to report started (nabuStarted, set by initCPU) and its SGI.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
index 76ed7b2..acc9a5c 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/NabuCPU.cpp
@@ -145,10 +145,13 @@ NabuCPU::startAll(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t result __unused)
 		if (cpu == NULL) {
 			panic("NABU CPU: missing nub for logical CPU %u", cpu_id);
 		}
-		kern_return_t kr = processor_start(cpu->machProcessor);
-		if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) {
-			panic("NABU CPU: processor_start cpu=%u failed: %d", cpu_id, kr);
-		}
+		/*
+		 * XNU 12377 without USE_APPLEARMSMP boots each processor from
+		 * ml_processor_register() (osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c), i.e. in
+		 * NabuCPU::start; processor_start() is a kext no-op returning
+		 * KERN_FAILURE and a second processor_boot() panics "already booted".
+		 * Only wait here for the CPU to report itself started.
+		 */
 		nanoseconds_to_deadline(5 * NSEC_PER_SEC, &deadline);
 		while (__atomic_load_n(&cpu->nabuStarted, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE) == 0 ||
 		    !nabu_cpu_signal_is_enabled(cpu_id)) {
